  {
    "question": "热蒸发型汞源在6英寸硅基HgCdTe外延生长中的作用是什么？",
    "source_file": "6英寸碲镉汞分子束外延设备汞束流仿真研究_吕文利_parsed.txt",
    "fragment_start": 1188,
    "fragment_end": 2188,
    "fragment_text": "ore device fabrication process of 6-inch silicon-based mercury cadmium telluride (HgCdTe) epitaxy faces challenges such as poor film uniformity and inadequate performance of mercury sources in domestically produced molecular beam epitaxy systems. There is an urgent need to develop a thermal evaporation-type $\\mathrm { H g }$ source. This paper employs multiphysics finite element simulation to investigate the influence of various structural parameters, including size and angle of the evaporation outlet aperture and crucible diameter, on the distribution, magnitude, and deposition uniformity of the $\\mathrm { H g }$ source’s emitted beam flux on a 6-inch substrate. Through optimization, the film thickness non-uniformity is reduced to below $1 . 2 3 \\%$ . This study offers insights and a theoretical basis for design and optimization of large-scale HgCdTe molecular beam epitaxy systems.\n\nKey words: molecular beam epitaxy equipment; Hg source; model simulation; optimization design\n\n红外探测器在军事",
    "chunk_labels": {
      "fixed": {
        "chunk_file": "6英寸碲镉汞分子束外延设备汞束流仿真研究_吕文利_parsed_chunk_2.txt",
        "overlap_ratio": 0.75
      },
      "semantic": {
