    "fragment_text": "urces. In order to meet the urgent demand, a tracked vehicle mobile miniaturized and digital radiography (DR) NDT testing system prototype based on S-band accelerator X-ray sources is developed by using modular, standardized and compact design concepts and methods, and the prototype performance is experimental tested. The experimental results show that the energy of the accelerator X-ray source in the system exceeds $2.8\\mathrm{MeV}$ , and the maximum dose rate at 1 meter in front of the target is $405\\mathrm{mGy / min}$ . The X-ray head of the prototype can be real-time adjusted for lifting and pitching, with a lifting range of 1.8 meters, and a pitching angle between $\\pm 45$ degrees. For DR detection, the system can detect parts with a height of more than 3 meters, and the maximum detectable equivalent steel thickness is not less than $120\\mathrm{mm}$ . The detection sensitivity of the system is better than $1\\%$ when examined by an image quality meter.\n\nKeywords: S-band, Accelerato",
